      "writtenOn": "2024-07-09T15:38:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right; pointers won\u0027t themselves be 16-byte aligned. I had been thinking about std::max_align_t, which can be 16, and thinking that `SkAlignPtr` would produce a value that was an aligned address, not a value that could hold a `void*` value.",
      "parentUuid": "d6d8dd4f_228f6ffa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 56,
